  "description": "COADM01C performs no dataset access whatsoever - it contains no SELECT, no FD, no EXEC CICS READ, STARTBR, READNEXT, WRITE, REWRITE or DELETE, and its five EXEC CICS statements are one RETURN, one SEND MAP and one RECEIVE MAP. That absence is behaviour and this case asserts it positively rather than by omission: the security file IS seeded, at the eighty bytes app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy declares, so it is present and readable throughout the run - and both record channels of the fingerprint must still come back completely empty, with no dataset named on either. Seeding without expecting is the whole point; a case that simply omitted the dataset could not tell 'the unit read nothing' from 'nobody looked'. The rows are the in-stream data of app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl, whose literal SEC-USR-PWD span is the legacy design's placeholder value and not a credential; COADM01C never reads it.",
